meta {
  name: Delete Referral Doctor
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/referral-doctors/{{referralDoctorId}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

vars:pre-request {
  referralDoctorId: 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
}

docs {
  🔒 **RBAC:** requires `branch_admin:referrals__delete_referral_doctor` — enforced by `PermissionGuard` (`@RequirePermission`). A caller whose effective permissions (user override ?? branch-role override ?? role baseline) lack this get **403 `PERMISSION_DENIED`**; the `business_admin` / `administrator` roles bypass all checks, so `{{businessAccessToken}}` (an admin) still succeeds here.
  
  Soft-delete a referral doctor (sets `deletedAt`) and cascade soft-deletes its
  active qualifications, experiences, and assigned lab tests/panels, in one
  transaction. Scoped to the caller's tenant. 404 `REFERRAL_DOCTOR_NOT_FOUND` if
  missing, already soft-deleted, or owned by another tenant.

  **409 `REFERRAL_DOCTOR_IN_USE`** — deletion is blocked when the doctor is used by
  an order still in an active accessioning/technician-stage workflow (a non-cancelled
  order with a sample still being collected/processed, or a lab report not yet published). Deactivate the doctor
  instead (`PATCH` with `status: INACTIVE`). Historical / fully-published / cancelled
  orders do **not** block deletion.
}
